{
  "title": "Show derived grams first in ingredient lines ('~120 g (1 cup) flour')",
  "description": "Owner's house style puts weights first: '120 g (1 cup) flour'. \
Grams are already derived on read from the catalog (ramekin-core/src/volume_to_weight.rs derived_grams, returned as derived measurements) and never stored, so catalog fixes reach every recipe. \
Today both clients show them after the source's measure: '1 cup (~120 g) flour'. \
The owner chose to get grams-first as a deterministic display change rather than having the house_style AI op rewrite stored amounts (decided 2026-10-25 while unblocking normalize-3). \
Change web ramekin-ui/src/utils/ingredientFormatting.ts and iOS Ingredient.formatted(scale:includeAlternatives:includeNote:derived:) so a line with derived grams leads with them: '~120 g (1 cup) flour'. \
Lines with no derived grams ('1 egg', 'salt to taste', a line already in grams) are unchanged. \
Scaling must still scale both. \
This is pure client logic on both clients: pin it with shared test vectors in shared-test-vectors/ (the ingredient formatting vectors IngredientFormattingSharedVectorTests already reads) per doc/client-logic-sharing.md. \
No make pipeline diff expected.",
